{
  "format": 1,
  "conventions": {
    "canvas": "Each scene is a folder: background.svg is 1920 by 1080; every other layer is a prop SVG at its own size.",
    "size": "Props are drawn at real size for the characters: about 265 px to the metre at the floor (an adult at scale 0.5 is about 450 px, 1.7 m). A prop's feet rest on the centre line of the soft contact shadow at the bottom of its SVG; its layer y puts that line on floorY (or on the top of the furniture it sits on). The background is drawn in perspective with the horizon about 1.5 m above floorY, so what stands farther back is smaller.",
    "layers": "Layers are listed bottom to top. x and y are the layer's centre in movie pixels from the top-left of the 1920 by 1080 movie; scale multiplies the SVG's own size.",
    "floorY": "floorY is where feet rest, in movie pixels. A starter character placed at scale 0.5 stands on the floor when its centre is at y = floorY - 236.",
    "camera": "camera is the movie camera's starting preset: panX and panY in movie pixels, zoom 1 for the full frame.",
    "elements": "Only path, rect, circle, ellipse, line, polyline and polygon with solid fills (fill-opacity for soft shadows and light), strokes and linear or radial gradients in defs. No text, filters, masks, patterns, images or CSS.",
    "license": "Original artwork made for this project and covered by the repository's own license."
  },
